  When the signal hits, we wake up, without any signal\n215:   // handlers being invoked.\n216:   int signal_number = signals.Wait(info);\n217:   if (!ShouldHalt()) {\n218:     // Let the user know we got the signal, just in case the system's too screwed for us to\n219:     // actually do what they want us to do...\n220:     LOG(INFO) << *self << \": reacting to signal \" << signal_number;","truncated_fields":["content"]}
